### Endpoints for the front ends

The app has an endpoint for each operation of an exposed API
(`expose: true`), so that a front end can use the API without its
secret. The path of an endpoint is `/apis/<api>/<operation>` in kebab
case, for example `{{ exposed[0].prefix }}{{ exposed[0].methods[0].endpoint_path }}`, and
its method is the method of the operation. The endpoint takes the
parameters of the operation as query parameters, and the body of the
operation as its body. An error of the API gives 502.
